DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ffcc--ppaatttteerrnn parses _p_a_t_t_e_r_n (empty pattern  by  default)  and  shows  the
       parsed  result.  If ----ccoonnffiigg is given, config substitution is performed
       on the pattern before being displayed.  If ----ddeeffaauulltt is given,  default
       substitution is performed on the pattern before being displayed.

       If any elements are specified, only those are printed.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       This  program  follows the usual GNU command line syntax, with long op‐
       tions starting with two dashes (`-'). A summary of options is  included
       below.

       --cc     Perform config substitution on pattern.

       --dd     Perform default substitution on pattern.

       --ff     Format output according to the format specifier _f_o_r_m_a_t.

       --VV     Show version of the program and exit.

       --hh     Show summary of options.

       _p_a_t_t_e_r_n
              Parses and displays _p_a_t_t_e_r_n (uses empty pattern by default).

       _e_l_e_m_e_n_t
              If set, the _e_l_e_m_e_n_t property is displayed for parsed pattern.

